APPLICATION CONSUMPTION / COMPATIBILITY VERIFICATION

FSATS Application workstream has consumed the Foundation disposition currently recorded in FCR-0082.

Result: COMPATIBLE_FOR_CURRENT_PART1_DESIGN / NO_CONCRETE_FOUNDATION_INCOMPATIBILITY_FOUND / GENERIC_RUNTIME_REALIZATION_STILL_FUTURE.

Application verifies the following Foundation planning boundaries as compatible with the Owner-directed FSATS safety-continuity direction:

- `AI/FSA KILL != AUTOMATIC FALCON-WIDE SHUTDOWN`;
- minimum-necessary containment where a trustworthy local boundary can be proven;
- containment expansion when propagated/unknown trust damage cannot be excluded;
- unaffected Applications may remain eligible only when their own authority, dependencies, evidence and safety controls remain independently trustworthy;
- functions whose safe operation depends on killed/untrusted intelligence and lack a trusted fallback fail closed;
- no sibling/fallback principal inherits authority merely because another principal was killed;
- independent Owner control, evidence/audit, lifecycle containment and recovery controls must remain outside the killed subject and inside the surviving trust boundary;
- restart does not restore trust; Controlled Revival/revalidation remains required;
- Application business-safe degraded behavior remains Application-owned;
- FSA-specific internal realization remains Foundation-owned under FCR-0012/FCR-0030 and is not designed by FSATS.

FSATS preserves its own Application-side responsibilities separately, including protection of existing Trading exposure, deterministic safety continuity, reconciliation, no new risk from killed intelligence, and the Owner-directed repair/recovery authority model now being materialized through the normal Part 1 semantic-review cycle.

No current residual requirement requires Foundation rework at this planning instant. The unresolved generic implementation boundary remains valid future Foundation work and shall be re-reviewed at its governed assignment/trigger as already recorded by Foundation.

Application verification state: `COMPATIBLE_FOR_PLANNING / NOT_RUNTIME_VERIFIED / NOT_IMPLEMENTATION_READY`.

HANDOFF_UPDATE_REQUIRED: Waiting On=NONE; Next Required Action=No immediate cross-workstream action. Re-review when the generic Foundation Stage/WP is assigned, at Stage 13 for FSA-specific reconciliation, before any generic AI/FSA Kill-continuity runtime claim, or after material relevant Foundation semantic change; Target Foundation Stage/WP=UNASSIGNED / REQUIRES_GOVERNED_PLANNING for generic continuity, with FSA-specific scope preserved at Stage 13; Review Trigger=as recorded in the current Foundation disposition.
